# Get Started
---------------
To get started with Android/LineageOS, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

# Initialize local repository

To initialize your local repository using the AetheriaOS trees, use a command like this:
```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/AetheriaOS/aetheria_manifest.git -b aetheria-1.0
```
# Sync up

Then to sync up:
```bash
repo sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags --force-sync -j8
```
# Set up environment

Set up the build environment
```bash
. build/envsetup.sh
```
# Lunch target

Lunch a target
```bash
lunch aetheria_codename-bp4a-userdebug
```

# Start compiling

```bash
m bacon -j$(nproc)
```

# Building as Official Maintainer
---------------
> **Note:** Only registered maintainers in [AetheriaOS Official Devices](https://github.com/AetheriaOS/aetheria_official_devices) can build official releases.

Make sure your SSH key is registered in your GitHub account, then build as usual. The build system will automatically detect your GitHub username and mark the build as **OFFICIAL**.

To verify your SSH key is working:
```bash
ssh -T git@github.com
```
Expected output:

Then build normally:
```bash
. build/envsetup.sh
lunch aetheria_codename-bp4a-userdebug
m bacon -j$(nproc)
```

The build will automatically be marked as:
- **OFFICIAL** — if your GitHub username is registered in official devices repo
- **UNOFFICIAL** — if your GitHub username is not registered
